---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Feature from '../components/Feature.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { team } from '../data/site';

import teamPhoto from '../assets/team-counter.jpg';
import harbourBoat from '../assets/harbour-boat-bw.jpg';
import jamieSpread from '../assets/jamie-spread.jpg';
import counterCustomers from '../assets/counter-customers.jpg';
import counterCreels from '../assets/counter-creels.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story"
  description="Four generations from Morecambe Bay to Borough Market — the Salisbury family, the team behind the counter, and why we still do it the slow way."
  transparentHeader
>
  <Hero
    image={teamPhoto}
    alt="The Furness Fish Market team behind the counter at Borough Market"
    eyebrow="Our story"
    title="Four generations of getting up early"
    lede="A Morecambe Bay shrimping family who took the long way to London — and brought the standards with them."
    position="center 35%"
  />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap wrap--mid" data-reveal>
      <p class="lede">
        There is no clever origin story here. No brand consultant, no pivot. Just a family who have
        been pulling things out of cold British water for the better part of a century, and who
        decided — somewhere around 1998 — that London deserved to see what that actually looks like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Feature
    image={harbourBoat}
    alt="A working fishing boat moored at a harbour, photographed in black and white"
    eyebrow="Where it began"
    title="A horse, a cart, and the Morecambe sands"
  >
    <p>
      <strong>Leslie Salisbury Sr.</strong> fished Morecambe Bay for more than fifty years. He learned
      the brown shrimp beds from old Jack Butler, who worked the sands the way they had always been
      worked — with a horse and a cart, reading the tide by eye, and getting off the flats before it
      turned.
    </p>
    <p>
      What Leslie built from that became the largest and most respected potted shrimp business in the
      world. He is gone now. The recipe is not: we still pot Morecambe Bay brown shrimps in spiced
      butter, and we still do it his way.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature
    image={jamieSpread}
    alt="A spread from Jamie Oliver's Jamie's Kitchen featuring Les Salisbury holding a large monkfish"
    eyebrow="South, eventually"
    title="Ulverston, Barrow, Gretna, Penrith — then Southwark Street"
    flip
    caption="Les Salisbury in Jamie Oliver's Jamie's Kitchen"
  >
    <p>
      <strong>Les Salisbury</strong> started where his father did: shrimping the bay as a boy. He took
      the family trade across the north of England — market after market, town after town — before
      taking the biggest gamble of the lot and bringing it to London.
    </p>
    <p>
      Four decades in, he has built one of the most respected fish counters in the country. Jamie
      Oliver put the stall in <em>Jamie's Kitchen</em> and called the Borough traders the heroes of the
      market. Les would tell you that is overdoing it. Everyone else would tell you it is not.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <!-- ------------------------------------------------------------- team -- -->
  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="team__intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Behind the counter</p>
        <h2>The people who actually do it</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          A counter is only ever as good as the person standing behind it at half six in the morning,
          in the cold, arranging ice. These are ours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="team">
        {
          team.map((person, index) => (
            <li data-reveal data-reveal-delay={(index % 3) * 90}>
              <h3>{person.name}</h3>
              <p class="team__role">{person.role}</p>
              <p class="team__note">{person.note}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Feature
    image={counterCustomers}
    alt="Customers choosing fish across the Furness Fish Market counter"
    eyebrow="The pride bit"
    title="We would rather explain it than sell it"
  >
    <p>
      Nobody here works on commission. If the turbot is not right today, we will say so and point you
      at the hake instead. If you have never cooked a whole fish in your life, ask — someone will
      talk you through it for as long as it takes, and prep it however you need.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is not a service policy. It is just what happens when the people selling the fish are the
      same people who care whether your dinner works.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature
    image={counterCreels}
    alt="Lobster creels, driftwood and rope above the Furness fish display"
    eyebrow="Slow Food"
    title="Good, clean and fair — and we mean all three"
    flip
  >
    <p>
      We are proud members of the Slow Food movement, which in practice means we are willing to be
      slower and dearer than a supermarket in exchange for knowing exactly what we are selling and
      who caught it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Day boats over trawlers wherever we can. Hand-dived over dredged. British over flown, when
      British is better. Recyclable packaging where it exists. None of it is complicated — it is just
      a series of small decisions, taken honestly, every day since 1998.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <CtaBand
    image={teamPhoto}
    alt=""
    eyebrow="Come and say hello"
    title="Ask us anything. Genuinely, anything."
    position="center 35%"
  >
    <p class="lede">
      6 Southwark Street, Borough Market. Open Tuesday to Sunday, and someone on this list will be
      behind the counter every single one of those days.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn--light" href="/visit/">Plan your visit</a>
      <a class="btn btn--light" href="/the-counter/">See the counter</a>
    </div>
  </CtaBand>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .team__intro {
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .team {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .team li {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 1.35rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-on-dark);
  }
  .team h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 1.2rem + 0.9vw, 1.8rem);
  }
  .team__role {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--body);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.19em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brass-2);
  }
  .team__note {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted-on-dark);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .team { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .team { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
